                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1][b] Broadway: 1849 [/b][/h1]\n\n[b]A Different Type of Review for a Different Type of Game: [/b]\n\nThis game is different. It’s an earlier iteration of COG games, and by that metric it has an entirely different feel than some of its later counterparts. It’s race-blind (not the same as race inclusive), light on deep-characterization, and more interested in plots and stats. \n\n[h3] This game is: a love letter to the theater, and to the people of who love theater. \nThis game is: an expressway through a certain part of theater-history. \n This game is: fun, if you can, or want to, appreciate any of those things. [/h3]\n\nIf you are willing (re: eager) to experience this with these things in mind you’ll have a great time. \nI did! The theater nerd in me made doe eyes at the references.",
